    "body": "I'm not the hugest fan of this wording because it's not obvious what it means to `set -o functrace` while initializing starship (does it need to be done concurrently?), and the presence of multiple **must** seems overbearing.\r\n\r\nPerhaps now that there are multiple requirements, it would be better to say something like \"note that there are requirements that must be observed around order and shell state when setting these functions, see code snippet for details\" and then move some of the prose into comments? That way, people will have a record of why things need to be a certain way if they choose to copy the code snippet.",
